  "notes": [
    "The seed, draws, fixtures, tolerance and minimums were registered in protocol v4 before any reference grid existed; v5 changed only the reference I/O before any v5 run.",
    "Protocol v4 failed on these draws because the reference grids were written to 9 decimals; that record is kept. Here inputs reach the reference as float64 binary and outputs are hex floats, both checked.",
    "The first v5 terra pass read the cell sizes from CSV, which R parsed one ulp off in five draws; the protocol requires exact inputs, so the sizes are read from cellsizes.f64. Compared values were the same in both passes.",
    "Even-count medians here are exact float32 ties, as in real LAS data after float32 ingest; every one agrees.",
    "Scope is measured cells only. Interpolated (IDW fill) cells are not covered.",
    "The numbers are computed by tests/dtmMedianCrossCheck.test.ts."
